528 - A Shelter in the Time of Storm
 / 
Key: F
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 528
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
[F]The Lord's our Rock, in [Gm]Him we hide, A [C]Shelter in the time of [F]storm;
[F]Secure whatever [Gm]may betide, A [C]Shelter in the time of [F]storm.
Mighty [Bb]Rock in a [F]weary land, Cooling shade on the [C]burning [F]sand,
Faithful [Bb]guide for the [F]pilgrim band- A shelter in the [C7]time of [F]storm.

Refrain:
[F]Mighty [Gm]Rock in [C]a [F]weary land,
[F]Cooling [Gm]shade on [C]the [F]burning sand,
[Bb]Faithful [F]guide for [C]the [F]pilgrim band--
[Bb]A [F]shelter in [C7]the time [F]of storm.

Verse 2:
[F]A [Gm]shade by [C]day, defense [F]by night,
[F]A [Gm]shelter in [C]the time [F]of storm;
[Bb]No [F]fears alarm, [C]no [F]foes afright,
[Bb]A [F]shelter in [C7]the time [F]of storm.

Verse 3:
[F]The [Gm]raging storms [C]may round [F]us beat,
[F]A [Gm]shelter in [C]the time [F]of storm
[Bb]We'll [F]never leave [C]our [F]safe retreat,
[Bb]A [F]shelter in [C7]the time [F]of storm.

Verse 4:
[F]O [Gm]Rock divine, [C]O [F]Refuge dear,
[F]A [Gm]Shelter in [C]the time [F]of storm;
[Bb]Be [F]Thou our [C]helper [F]ever near,
[Bb]A [F]Shelter in [C7]the time [F]of storm.
